==Battleground==
*10 [[Croconator]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Capy]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Luke (Enemy)|Luke]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Capy]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**2 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**20 [[Croconator]]s spawn, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**3 [[Zigge]]s spawn, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
**1 [[Guile (Enemy)|Guile]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A rather interesting stage, although not as difficult as the 12-Star rating suggests. This stage consists of mainly meatshields, with Luke and Guile acting as punishing backliners. Fortunately, both Luke and Guile are vulnerable to snipers such as [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] or [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]. Include a few meatshields in your lineup as well as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] to deal with the Capys. Zigge can be a problem with their burrowing, but this can be mitigated with [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] if you are struggling. Something to deal with the Dark Otters, such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], will be very helpful.

Also note that if using [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] or Esoteric Uril they both need a stepping stone to hit Luke and Guile, although this shouldn't be an issue with the constant spam of Croconators.

